<p>  per share	  9,721,693  9,697,611  9,721,693  9,697,611</p>
<p>(A)  During the first quarter of 1995, the company incurred an extraordinary loss as a result of the early retirement of its outstanding 10.42 percent senior notes.  </p>
<p>The outstanding notes were retired on January 24, 1995 from the net proceeds received from the sale of $125 million of unsecured 10-7/8 percent senior notes due February 1, 2005.</p>
<p>(B)  As a result of decreased crude oil requirements at the Pasadena refinery, the company achieved a reduction in LIFO inventories during the third and fourth quarters of 1996. The impact of the LIFO inventory reduction and certain adjustments to base inventory values was to reduce the net loss by about $13.1 million ($1.34 per share) and by about $3 million ($.31 per share) for the twelve months ended December 31, 1996 and 1995, respectively.</p>
